  "scope_of_inference": "One word-final expansion selected from the 48 most frequent Czech 2- and 3-letter suffixes, with the four predefined EVA-basic cth, ckh, cph and cfh signs. Internal instances have no reading, including the earlier sign in a consecutive pair. The search fits single-unit readings before suffix fitting and then uses the stock lexical coordinate sweeps. Glyph mappings are selected on the public practice training partition alone. The pooled Early Modern and 19th-century Czech material does not model medieval spelling or other choices of abbreviation signs and endings. The stock synthetic controls plant one-to-one ordinary glyph mappings because the 26-letter ASCII target uses all non-reserved control glyphs. The four planted forms are ho, li, ti and ch. A single-Kralice plaintext control still uses the same pooled reference training and suffix lists. The search does not distinguish folded diacritics.",
  "reference_sources": {
    "training_method": "Pooled 400-character blocks over both active pins. In the pooled reference, 8,348 of 8,405 blocks come from the Kralice text.",
